# Terminal Component Blueprint

All new components must inherit the terminal-modern aesthetic using these utilities. Do not manually restyle; use the blueprint classes.

## Base Identity

- **`.terminal-base`** - Foundation for all components: card background, border, radius, padding, foreground color, sans font.
- **`.terminal-surface`** - Panel identity: inset highlight + texture + 1px top border (green dim). Use for panel-like components.
- **`.terminal-panel`** - Inset highlight only.
- **`.terminal-panel-texture`** - Subtle noise overlay.

## Spacing

- **`.stack-sm`** - Small vertical gap (0.5rem).
- **`.stack-md`** - Medium vertical gap (1rem). Default for new components.
- **`.stack-lg`** - Large vertical gap (1.5rem).

## Typography

- **`.terminal-heading`** - Display font, headings.
- **`.terminal-subheading`** - Display font, subheadings.
- **`.terminal-body`** - Body text, muted foreground.
- **`.terminal-mono`** - Monospace elements.

## Code Blocks

- **`.code-block-terminal`** - Elevated background, inset highlight, monospace, dim green top accent.

## CTAs

- **`.btn-primary`** / **`.btn-terminal-primary`** - Green background, black text.
- **`.btn-ghost`** / **`.btn-terminal-ghost`** - Transparent, subtle border.

## Sections

- **`.terminal-section`** - Section shell: padding, max-width, centering, subtle depth.

## Default for New Components

When creating a new component, include by default:

- `.terminal-base` (or `.terminal-surface` if panel-like)
- `.terminal-panel` + `.terminal-panel-texture` (if panel)
- `.stack-md` for vertical rhythm
- `.terminal-body` for text
- `.terminal-heading` for titles

## Do Not Modify

- ScrollMotion, ScrollStagger, TypingSequence, BootSequence
- Animation timing or motion logic
- Component structure or layout
